# The enforcement surface. The leading catch-all is deliberate: lint escapes
# and mutation classifications can live anywhere, so every change needs the
# owner's review. The named paths below repeat it for the files that hold the
# gate itself. Cargo.toml is unanchored on purpose: member crate manifests
# carry the `[lints] workspace = true` opt-in, so adding one is a wall edit.
# tests/allow_policy.rs and tests/lint_wall.rs read the Rust task fragment
# from .config/mise/conf.d/; move their path with it.
* @TheLunchTrae
/.cargo/ @TheLunchTrae
/.config/mise/ @TheLunchTrae
/.github/ @TheLunchTrae
/AGENTS.md @TheLunchTrae
Cargo.toml @TheLunchTrae
